This confirms it. The `else` branch for single-selection options (`option.lookupValue(context.getUser(), value)` where `value` could be `null` when the parameter isn't provided) was introduced in commit `b1940a88bf7e10bc2ec8dcc19d5120ffd98d2690`, with no null-check on `value` before calling `option.lookupValue()` / `Long.valueOf(value)`. This is exactly the code path later fixed in `944abee6` by wrapping it in `if (value != null) { ... }`.

## Bug-Introducing Commits
BIC: b1940a88bf7e10bc2ec8dcc19d5120ffd98d2690

## Reasoning
(1) I used `git log --follow -p` on the affected file to see its history, then `git blame` on the parent of the fix commit for the exact lines touched by the fix. All the modified lines (the `else` branch handling single-selection HQL report options) blamed to a single commit, `b1940a88bf`.

(2) That commit introduced the entire block:
```java
String value = helper.getParameter(option.name());
SavedHQLInterface.IdValue v = new SavedHQLInterface.IdValue();
v.setValue(option.name());
Long id = option.lookupValue(context.getUser(), value);
if (id == null) {
    try { id = Long.valueOf(value); } catch (NumberFormatException e) {}
}
v.setText(id == null ? "" : id.toString());
params.add(v);
```
Here `value` comes from `helper.getParameter(option.name())`, which can legitimately be `null` when the request doesn't supply that particular option parameter. The original code unconditionally creates an `IdValue`, calls `option.lookupValue(..., value)` with a null value, and adds a param entry regardless — meaning an unset option still gets added to `params` with an empty/garbage text. The bug-fix commit wraps the whole block in `if (value != null) { ... }`, skipping option creation entirely when the parameter wasn't provided, which is the correct behavior and exactly undoes the defect from `b1940a88bf`.

(3) The diff of `b1940a88bf` (shown above) is a near-identical match to the pre-fix code at `944abee6^`, and `git blame` directly attributes every line altered by the fix to this single commit. No intervening commit touched this block (per the `git log --follow -p` commit list, the next touch to this file was `e759bfe25c`, which only added unrelated code after this block). I'm confident this is the bug-introducing commit.

